From: Caner Altinbasak <cal@brightsign.biz>
Date: Mon, 13 Apr 2026 09:37:51 +0100
Subject: ozone/nexus: Assign VirtualKeyboard role to overlay windows OS-20973

Tooltip, popup, and menu windows were created without a Nexus surface
role (eNone). After the SetZOrderLevel changes gave the main window a
Graphics role, libbscompositor's role-based z-ordering placed the
role-less overlay windows behind the graphics surface.

Fix by assigning NEXUS_BrightSignSurfaceRole_eVirtualKeyboard to
tooltip, popup, and menu windows at creation time. In the compositor's
arrangement order (video > graphics > subtitles > ticker > virtual
keyboard > cursor), this ensures overlays appear above the main
graphics content.

diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/nexus/nexus_window.cc b/ui/ozone/platform/nexus/nexus_window.cc
index fc985bd218a477a7021adcf3bca8a05ee2d07a25..229c1298664b068eff1ebd9b7059c6230dadc612 100644
--- a/ui/ozone/platform/nexus/nexus_window.cc
+++ b/ui/ozone/platform/nexus/nexus_window.cc
@@ -80,6 +80,17 @@ NexusWindow::NexusWindow(PlatformWindowDelegate* delegate,
   win_info.height = bounds_.height();
   win_info.colorBlend = HideSourceColor;
   win_info.alphaBlend = HideSourceAlpha;
+
+  // Overlay window types (tooltips, popups, menus) need a role that sorts
+  // above graphics in the Nexus surface compositor's role-based z-ordering.
+  // Without a role they remain as eNone and get stuck behind role-bearing
+  // surfaces like the main graphics window.
+  if (properties.type == PlatformWindowType::kTooltip ||
+      properties.type == PlatformWindowType::kPopup ||
+      properties.type == PlatformWindowType::kMenu) {
+    win_info.role = NEXUS_BrightSignSurfaceRole_eVirtualKeyboard;
+  }
+
   native_window_ = NXPL_CreateNativeWindowEXT(&win_info);
 
   activatable_ = properties.activatable;
